/**
 * Copyright (c) 2026 AppleWOA authors.
 *
 * Module Name:
 *     CSRT.aslc
 *
 * Abstract:
 *     Core System Resource Table for the T8142 family (Apple M5).
 *
 *     *** NOT IMPLEMENTED, AND NOT PART OF THE BUILD. ***
 *
 *     This file is deliberately empty of table data. It is not listed in
 *     CPUAcpiTables.inf [Sources] and is not referenced by the FDF, so nothing
 *     here is compiled or emitted into the firmware volume. It exists to record
 *     the requirement, which is real.
 *
 * Why a CSRT would be needed:
 *
 *     Apple platforms implement some non-standard core system resources, namely
 *     the interrupt controller (AIC) and the IOMMU (DART). A CSRT is the ACPI
 *     mechanism for telling the OS that such non-enumerable resources exist so
 *     it can handle them correctly.
 *
 *     Note this project's approach makes the AIC half of that moot: m1n1
 *     emulates a GICv3 for the guest, so Windows sees a standard interrupt
 *     controller described by the MADT and never learns about the AIC. The DART
 *     side remains genuinely unaddressed -- anything needing DMA (storage, USB,
 *     display) will eventually need the IOMMU described somewhere.
 *
 *     The predecessor of this file in T810XFamilyPkg was identical: a comment
 *     block with no table. It was carried forward here rather than invented.
 *
 * Environment:
 *     UEFI firmware/runtime services.
 *
 * License:
 *     SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent OR MIT
 *
*/
